# Compiled binaries a developer may have left in the tree.
#
# Deliberately not `**/server`, which is what this said and which also matches
# every service's `cmd/server` *directory* — dockerignore patterns do not
# distinguish a file from a directory. That excluded the source of every
# binary in this repository from the build context, so `docker build` failed
# on `stat /src/<service>/cmd/server: directory not found` for all thirty-one
# services, and had since the Docker stack was first added.
#
# `*/server` matches one path segment before `server`, so it still catches
# `irrigation-service/server` from a stray `go build -o server`, and cannot
# reach `irrigation-service/cmd/server`.
/server
*/server
**/*.exe

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# IDE
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo

# Node / web build artifacts
web/node_modules
web/**/node_modules
web/**/dist
web/**/.next

# Mobile
mobile/.dart_tool
mobile/**/build
mobile/**/.flutter-plugins

# Rust build artifacts.
#
# By far the largest thing in this repository — ml-training/target alone runs
# to several gigabytes — and nothing a Go service image can use. Left in, every
# one of the thirty-one service builds copies all of it into the build context
# before the first instruction runs: slow in CI, and enough to exhaust the disk
# on a smaller machine.
#
# A glob rather than a list, so a new Rust crate is covered without anybody
# remembering to add it.
**/target/

# Python caches
python-ai/**/__pycache__
python-ai/**/*.pyc

# Documentation
**/*.md
!packages/**/README.md

# Test artifacts
**/*_test.go
**/tests/
**/testdata/

# Docker
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
